   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello,<br><br><div>I&#39;m trying to fit a random effects model. <br><br>Have students who have taken repeated tests.  Want to fit both an intercept and slope to each student.  (Perhaps an AR1 on the slope?)<br><br>When running the model below, I get an error of:<br>&quot;Error in if (nrep &gt; 1 || ngroup &gt; 1) { :<br>  missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>There is no missing data in my dataframe, and no NA values.</div><div><br></div><div>Any suggestions on how to resolve this?<br><br>Thank You!<br><br>The model is:</div><div>(Note:  student2 is just a direct copy of student)<br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255);font-family:&quot;Source Code Pro&quot;,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-weight:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;white-space:pre\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">m</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> &lt;- </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">inla</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">(</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">score</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(9,134,88)\">1</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">    + </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">f</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">student</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">model</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(163,21,21)\">&quot;iid&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">    + </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">f</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">student2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">replicate</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">student</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">model</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(163,21,21)\">&quot;ar1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">,  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">values</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(9,134,88)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(9,134,88)\">134</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">hyper</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">hyper1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">    , </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">data</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">df</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">family</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(163,21,21)\">&quot;gaussian&quot;</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">    , </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">control.compute</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">return.marginals.predictor</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">cpo</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,16,128)\">po</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">, </span><spa